#
# Clean conformance fixture for math:ConditionalIndependenceGivenShape (Rule P9): a
# math:ConditionalIndependenceAssertion A ⫫ B | C that names its subject
# (math:independenceSubject), the event it is independent of (math:independentOf), AND its
# conditioning set (math:independentGiven) — the C. All three events are measure-theoretic
# math:ProbabilityEvents (not typed logic:Event, so P11 stays satisfied). It MUST raise NO
# probability failure class.
# Positive counterpart of counter-examples/conditional-independence-ungiven.ttl.
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecConditionalIndependenceGiven).
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:givenIndependence a math:ConditionalIndependenceAssertion ;
    math:independenceSubject ex:symptomEvent ;
    math:independentOf ex:testEvent ;
    math:independentGiven ex:diseaseEvent .

ex:symptomEvent a math:ProbabilityEvent .
ex:testEvent a math:ProbabilityEvent .
ex:diseaseEvent a math:ProbabilityEvent .
